==Trivia==
*Heaven-Defying Fruit's Japanese name, Ten'i ni Somuku Rakka (天意に背く落果, "Fallen Fruit That Disobeys Heaven's Will"), may be a reference to the falling apple that inspired [[wikipedia:Isaac Newton|Isaac Newton]]'s gravitational theory.
**It may also reference the [[wikipedia:Fall of man|fall of mankind]] in Abrahamic religions, in which Adam and Eve ate the forbidden fruit of the tree of knowledge, disobeyed God, and fell from the Garden of Eden. This works with [[Restricted Area]]'s Japanese name, which can be translated as Forbidden Zone of Fluctuation.
*The team-up of [[Mistress Celeboodle]] and [[King Wahwah]] may reference their Japanese descriptions, which reveal that they form a [[wikipedia:Manzai|''manzai'']] comedy duo with Mistress Celeboodle as the ''tsukkomi'' (the short-tempered "straight man" who takes things seriously) and King Wahwah as the ''boke'' (the airheaded "funny man" who gets everything wrong).
**[[Oldstrich]], one of the two other enemies in the stage, also happens to be a comedian.
*[[Dogenstein]] is the only enemy in Heaven-Defying Fruit who is not described as a comedian in Japanese. His presence here along with the "Heaven-Defying" in the stage's name and ゆらぎ ''Yuragi'' (Fluctuation) in [[Restricted Area]]'s Japanese name may reference [[wikipedia:Albert Einstein|Albert Einstein]]'s quote criticizing quantum fluctuations, "[[wikipedia:Hidden-variable theory#"God does not play dice"|God does not play dice]]".

